You are given an integer n. On each step, you may subtract one of the digits from the number.
How many steps are required to make the number equal to 0?

Input:
The only input line has an integer n.

Output:
Print one integer: the minimum number of steps.

Constraints:
1<=n<=10^6

Strategy:
Here the main new thing is getting the digits out of a number. We can just take the number. Make a copy and then use num%10 to extract the last digit. Then, everytime we do num/=10 which removes the last digit. We can create a dp array sized n since each step we decrease by at least one. We initialize everything as 1e7 since we are finding a minimum and set dp[0]=0 since the number of steps to 0 from 0 is 0. Then we run a loop 1 to n and in each one use our digits extracting scheme as the inner loop and check dp[i]=min(dp[i-digit]+1,dp[i]). We output dp[n].